  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "When hand tracking is lost when in range of an object, the hand will go to its default resting position, but the lines showing that the object can be grabbed stay. The object grab line point to the hand after tracking is lost, so it will be pointed to the side. This will leave a floating line with no hand because the line won't touch the edge of the screen. Moving your head will move the line, so you could get the line across almost the whole display. I would expect that if hand tracking got lost you can not select anything so the grab object lines should not be shown until tracking is recovered. I see this more of a problem when you moving hands over each other, where sometimes it looses tracking, with no intention of picking up an object, they just happen to be around it and less of a problem when someone is trying to pick up an object. Sitting down and putting you hand on your knee in front of you is another time when tracking gets lost easy and this bug will show up. \nThis bug also shows up in the menu with the selection dot that shows what you are going to click on. When you loose tracking in the menu with your pointer on something you can move your head around and it will move the dot around and highlight buttons. You have no tracking so you can not select anything so it shouldn't be shown.",
